    {
      "object_id": "mathia_interpretation_e2a57463f75d5de1364440e1c7920003eb427ad66a06c566b7819869e4bc3ffd",
      "object_role": "interpretation",
      "proposed_content": "With RH held fixed, the passage compares what follows from RH alone with what follows after adding conjecture (2), then with Mueller's one stated weaker uniform upper bound: the added zero-ordinate statistic is thereby isolated as the input responsible for stronger prime-counting and prime-gap conclusions. This comparison gains a hierarchy of sufficient hypotheses and a reason to seek extensions, but loses any account of how the zero information reaches primes; that transfer and the exact quantitative bounds remain proof obligations, and every improvement stated here is conditional on RH plus the relevant extra hypothesis.",
      "parent_sources": [
        {
