    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_a8a552d8e0c3f8b6f4cd711cd59a5f98ffdf48a6fbb0f02d3e61687d108eb5b4",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Under RH, a smoothed short-interval prime variance is compared with a weighted zero-sum energy; expansion, symmetrization, truncation, and a logarithmic change of variables convert that energy into a localized transform of pair correlation. Averaging the interval scale confines the transform to the hypothesis range and yields a good parameter. Expanding the resulting nonnegative prime variance, accounting for background and diagonal mass, and using the sieve bound to exclude remote off-diagonal mass leaves positive central off-diagonal mass, which certifies a nearby distinct-prime pair.",
